<title>MALAYSIA: Tenaga to prioritise breakdown monitoring. [CORRECTED 8:28 GMT]</title>
<headline>Tenaga to prioritise breakdown monitoring. [CORRECTED 8:28 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline form &quot;privatise breakdown monitoring&quot;)</p>
<p>Utility firm Tenaga Nasional Bhd said on Friday it was privatising a huge project to monitor power breakdowns in remote areas of Malaysia.</p>
<p>Tenaga chairman Ahmad Tajuddin Ali said implementation of the system will cost 50 to 100 million ringgit annually up to the year 2001.</p>
</text>
